@{ ViewBag.Title="About HGRAS"; }
<main><section class="pgh-page-banner"><div class="pgh-wrap"><p class="pgh-eyebrow">Hospital Group Resource Allocation System</p><h1>One network.<br />More possibilities for care.</h1><p>The right resource, at the right hospital, at the right time.</p></div></section><div class="pgh-wrap pgh-page-grid"><section class="pgh-content"><img class="pgh-info-image" style="height:340px" src="@Url.Content("~/Content/img/hgras/hospital-exterior.jpg")" alt="Hospital facility exterior"/><h2>Make better use of what your group already has.</h2><p>HGRAS brings hospital groups, facilities, responsible officers and shared resources into one operational workspace. Teams can record stock, identify safely shareable quantities and coordinate transfers through approval, dispatch and confirmed receipt.</p><h2>Protect local care while supporting another hospital.</h2><p>Minimum reserves, expiry checks, hospital permissions and transactional reservations help prevent unsafe allocation. The audit trail records who requested a transfer, who authorised it and what happened at each handover.</p><h2>Keep decisions with the right people.</h2><p>Equipment, staffing, capacity and procurement records support coordination. Qualified officers remain responsible for clinical suitability, credentials, handling requirements and patient-transfer decisions.</p><a class="pgh-button" href="@Url.Action("Index","Network")">Open your hospital network →</a></section><aside class="pgh-info-card"><p class="pgh-eyebrow">Connected care operations</p><h2>Visibility with accountability.</h2><p>Hospital groups have separate memberships and workspaces. Hospital assignments control operational access. Recorded timestamps help teams understand how current their information is.</p><img class="pgh-info-image" src="@Url.Content("~/Content/img/hgras/clinical-team.jpg")" alt="Clinical team working together"/></aside></div></main>
